# Executed by build.py with the shared page and citation helpers.
gallery_g=json.loads((D/'gilinsky-gallery.json').read_text())
content=head('Gilinsky family / Benoni, Upington &amp; Johannesburg','A shopfront.<br>A family.<br>A life remembered.','Max and Riva, Shlomo’s Upington store and the siblings whose stories connect Benoni, Mayfair and Florida Lake.')
content+='<div class="branch-toolbar"><a href="#max-riva">Max &amp; Riva</a><a href="#shlomo-leah">Shlomo &amp; Leah</a><a href="#family-chart">Family chart</a><a href="#photographs">Photographs</a><a href="#next-research">Open questions</a></div>'
content+=img('gil-store.jpg','Shlomo standing outside a shop signed S. Gilinsky, General Dealer','Shlomo outside his Upington store, identified and located by Mark Cohen. Date unknown.','gil-store','gil-hero')
content+='<div class="reading-width prose">'
content+=section('Benoni, then Upington',p('Mark confirms that the Gilinsky family lived in <strong>Benoni before moving to Upington</strong>. The date of the move remains unknown. Gidon Katz’s account of his mother Milly’s childhood independently recalls this sequence. The store photograph preserves a concrete part of that world: the sign <strong>S. Gilinsky — General Dealer</strong>. The identification of the man as Shlomo and the location as Upington come from Mark.','gil-mark','gil-katz','gil-store')+img('gil-horse.jpg','Max Gilinsky on horseback in Upington','Mackie on horseback in Upington, identified by Mark. No date is written into the record.','gil-horse'))
content+=section('Max and Riva',p('<a href="people.html#max">Max (Mackie) Gilinsky</a> and <a href="people.html#riva">Riva (Masie / Mazie) Milstein</a> married in <strong>Johannesburg on 25 December 1938</strong>. Certificate 595 gives Max’s age as 28 and occupation as general dealer; Riva is 19, Poland-born and a typist. Her mother supplied consent. The record links this branch to the <a href="branch.html">Milstein–Lederer story</a>.','gil-max-marriage')+p('Mark recalls that Max owned <strong>Station Jewellers on Station Street, Mayfair</strong>, for many years. Katz’s published recollection names a watch and jewellery business belonging to Maxie Gilinsky, supporting the trade and neighbourhood. It does not provide the trading name, street number or opening and closing dates. Those remain research questions.','gil-mark','gil-katz')+img('gil-lake.jpg','Max and Riva sitting together at Florida Lake','Max and Riva at Florida Lake. Identification and location supplied by Mark; date unknown.','gil-lake')+p('The burial register records Max’s death on <strong>3 June 2000</strong>, burial the next day, and Hebrew name Mordecai son of Shlomo. Riva died and was buried on <strong>1 June 2015</strong>. Their graves adjoin. Max’s precise birth date of 1 October 1910 remains a family-tree entry rather than a birth record inspected here.','gil-max-stone','ethan'),id='max-riva')
content+=section('Shlomo and Leah: names across records',p('Mark identifies <a href="people.html#shlomo-gilinsky">Shlomo</a> as Max’s father. The matching civil death registration names <strong>Solomon Gilinsky</strong>, a general dealer, who died on <strong>24 August 1956</strong> at 101 Ninth Avenue, Mayfair. M. Gilinsky signed as the person arranging burial; the form does not explicitly call him a son. The gravestone gives the Hebrew name <strong>Shlomo son of Eliezer</strong>.','gil-mark','gil-sol-death','gil-sol-stone')+callout('A birth date that needs resolving',p('The supplied tree gives <strong>12 December 1885, Dvinsk</strong>. The death registration says <strong>80</strong> and the stone says <strong>79</strong>, pointing roughly to 1875–1877. A 1921 Upington marriage candidate gives age 40, implying about 1881. These are conflicting sources, not interchangeable dates. The civil death form says Russia; it does not independently establish Dvinsk.','ethan','gil-sol-death','gil-sol-stone','gil-sol-remarriage'))+p('A 1918 court catalogue names <strong>Solomon Gilinsky versus Leah Dinah, born Nasatir</strong>. A Johannesburg marriage register then records <strong>Leah Dinah Gilinsky, born Nasatir</strong>, a divorcee aged 41, marrying Jacob Mowsovitz on <strong>12 May 1920</strong>. These records strongly identify the court-case party, but a direct original linking her to Max is still needed. Anne Spiro’s estate index names her parents as Solomon and Lea Gilinsky.','gil-divorce','gil-leah-marriage','gil-anne-estate')+p('The Upington register records a divorced general dealer named <strong>Solomon Gilinsky marrying Rachel Skop, a widow, on 17 December 1921</strong>. This is a plausible remarriage of Max’s father, but it has not yet been linked through named children or an estate. The unidentified woman in the early family photograph should therefore not automatically be named Leah or Rachel.','gil-sol-remarriage','gil-mark'),id='shlomo-leah')
content+='</div>'
content+=section('A working family chart','<p>Gidon Katz describes two brothers and four sisters. The six names below fit that count and the recorded family conversation. The chart is a research reconstruction, not proof that one document names all six. Order below is not birth order.</p>'+cite('gil-katz','recent')+'<div class="gil-family"><div class="gil-parents"><a href="people.html#shlomo-gilinsky"><strong>Shlomo / Solomon Gilinsky</strong><span>Died 24 August 1956</span></a><a href="people.html#leah-gilinsky"><strong>Leah</strong><span>Candidate: Leah Dinah Nasatir</span></a></div><p class="gil-connection">Six siblings reconstructed from family accounts and separate records</p><div class="gil-siblings">'+''.join(f'<a href="people.html#{id}"><strong>{name}</strong><span>{text}</span><small>{status}</small></a>' for id,name,text,status in [('solly-gilinsky','Solly','Wife Sarah Gayer / Geyer','Brother in family account; father Shlomo on stone'),('max','Max (Mackie)','Husband of Riva Milstein','Identified by Mark; marriage inspected'),('milly-gilinsky','Milly','Wife of Max Katz','Mother identified by Gidon Katz'),('annie-gilinsky','Annie / Anne','Wife of Jack / Jacob Spiro','Marriage inspected; parentage from estate index'),('edie-gilinsky','Edith (Edie)','Married surname Lang','Strong sister candidate; father Shlomo on stone'),('fanny-gilinsky','Fanny','Wife of Bennie Lang','Marriage inspected; strong sister candidate')])+'</div></div>',id='family-chart')
content+='<div class="reading-width prose">'
content+=section('The Lang connections',p('Edith’s gravestone calls her <strong>Edith (Edie) Lang</strong>, names father Shlomo, and gives death on <strong>31 January 1956, aged 53</strong>. A Gazette notice establishes her maiden surname as Gilinsky and her residence at <strong>Rand Leases, Florida</strong>. Her estate number is <strong>1336/56</strong>. These details make her a strong candidate for Max’s sister. The Edith–Morris marriage has not been located.','gil-edie-stone','gil-edie-gazette')+p('<strong>Fanny Gilinsky married Bennie Lang on 25 November 1937</strong> in Johannesburg. Both were Mayfair residents; she was a saleslady aged 24 and he a Lithuania-born salesman aged 32. Fanny’s stone gives death on <strong>23 January 1987</strong> and a Hebrew patronymic naming Shlomo. Bennie’s stone names wife Fanny and gives death on <strong>7 October 1976</strong>.','gil-fanny-marriage','gil-fanny-stone','gil-bennie-stone')+p('The family conversation recalls relationships involving Edith, Fanny, Morris and Bennie. A Morris Lang burial entry gives death on 1 May 1973, in the grave numbered immediately after Edith’s. This is a lead, not proof of marriage or brotherhood. No later marriage or partnership between Fanny and Morris has been established.','recent','gil-morris-register','gil-bennie-stone'))
content+=section('Annie and Solly',p('Annie’s original Upington marriage is dated <strong>4 December 1929</strong>. Jack Spiro was 29, Ireland-born and a commercial traveller; Annie was 21 and South Africa-born. A candidate estate index for Anne Spiro gives parents Solomon and Lea Gilinsky, husband Jacob Spiro, birth year 1908 and death on 28 April 2007. The original estate image is unavailable, so those later details remain index-derived.','gil-annie-marriage','gil-anne-estate')+p('Solly’s stone gives <strong>25 December 1978</strong>, names wife Sarah and the Hebrew patronymic Israel son of Shlomo. A marriage index records Solly and Sarah Gayer on <strong>24 June 1928</strong>. Katz calls her Sara Geyer and connects her and sister Eva with the Ochberg group; the original marriage and immigration evidence still need closer inspection. Sarah’s stone gives <strong>27 June 1991</strong> and father Eliyahu.','gil-solly-stone','gil-solly-marriage','gil-katz','gil-sarah-stone'))
content+='</div>'
familyphotos=[x for x in gallery_g if x[3] in ['gil-store','gil-horse','gil-lake']]
# Additional family photographs, including groups with deliberately unnamed children.
content+=section('Photographs and the people still unnamed','<p>Family identifications are credited to Mark Cohen. No child has been named through facial comparison. Dates and unidentified people stay open for inscriptions, family recollections or records to resolve.</p><div class="gallery">'+''.join(img(file,title,caption,source) for file,title,caption,source in familyphotos+json.loads((D/'gilinsky-extra-photos.json').read_text()))+'</div>',id='photographs')
content+=section('Records behind this branch','<p>Open the saved file or follow its citation to the archive. FamilySearch viewer captures are labelled screenshots; they are not original-resolution downloads.</p><div class="chapter-grid">'+''.join('<article><h3>'+title+'</h3>'+p(note,id)+'<a href="assets/documents/'+sd[id]['file']+'">Open saved record</a></article>' for id,title,note in [('gil-max-marriage','Max and Riva, 1938','Marriage register, saved viewer screenshot.'),('gil-fanny-marriage','Fanny and Bennie, 1937','Marriage register, saved viewer screenshot.'),('gil-leah-marriage','Leah Dinah, 1920','Remarriage register, saved viewer screenshot.'),('gil-sol-death','Solomon, 1956','Civil death registration, saved viewer screenshot.')])+'</div>')
content+=section('What the next records could resolve','<div class="three-up"><article><h3>Solomon’s estate</h3>'+p('TAB MHG 6258/56 may name spouses, children, parents and birthplace. An enquiry was sent on 20 November 2026; the file has not been received.','gil-estate')+'</article><article><h3>Edith and the Lang marriages</h3>'+p('Obtain estate 1336/56 and locate Edith’s marriage. Her estate number falls between FamilySearch’s displayed 1333–1335 and 1338 ranges. That is a coverage gap, not a missing-file finding.','gil-edie-gazette')+'</article><article><h3>Station Jewellers and photograph dates</h3>'+p('Look for dated directories, advertisements, shop papers and writing on photo backs. The trading years and unnamed children remain unresolved.','gil-mark')+'</article></div>',id='next-research')
page('gilinsky.html','The Gilinsky family',content)
